Recently, Norman J. Meluch gave a summary of his reactions to some of the 
polymorph taming proposals floating about on the net.  In the interest of
keeping the issue current, here is a list of all the limitation proposals
that I have seen since about two months ago.  

(If *you* have a proposal that is not on this list, or would like to add
or retract support from the ideas as given here, please feel free to email
or flame me as desired.)

-Leonard			Help stamp out polypiling in our lifetime!



1) Poof!
Give polymorph a % chance to destroy an object
	ncalvin@oracle.uucp (Nate Calvin)
	cah@jpl-devvax.jpl.nasa.gov (Allen Halsell)
	pvk@tolsun.oulu.fi (Pertti Kotipalo)
	zeiglea@prism.cs.orst.edu (Anthony Zeigler)

2) Entropy
Give all items a power level, and insure that items are never polymorphed
into items of higher power.
	leonard@mimsy.umd.edu (Leonard Dickens)


3) Drudgery
Randomly disperse polymorphed objects throughout the known dungeon -
forcing the polypiler to trudge around again to build the pile up again.
	schnable@cbnewsc.att.com (andrew.schnable)


4) Creep, creep
Make polymorph only affect the top N items on up to M piles.  The most
common suggestions here are N=1,M=1 and N=1,M=5.
	sma@devcom.com.UUCP (Steve Adams)
	kevin@rotag.uucp (Kevin Darcy)

4.1) Crawl, crawl
Make polymorph only affect N% of the stuff it is aimed at.
	kevin@stl.stc.co.uk (K.Lewis)

4.2) Get real!
Limit piles of objects to size consistent with their floor area.


5) I wish...
Make polymorph explicitly equivalent to wishing, maybe more limited in the
range of items you could get.  This might require polymorph control.
	prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts)
	dsmith@spam.ua.oz.au (David Smith)


6) Scarlet Letter
Leave polymorph alone, but flag all high scorers who use it, or put the scores
into separate (but equal) files.

6.1) More major modes
Make a special demi-god mode, with lots of limits on things that people find
abusive.  Combine this with (10)


7) Gotta run!
Put time bonuses into the scoring system, so that a player who spends the time
to set up really big piles would be penalized accordingly.
	pippin@leland.Stanford.EDU (Michael Killianey)


8) Fizzle, fizzle.
Make polymorph unable to generate polymorph, in either wand or book form.


9) Squish, squish.
Make polymorph only affect things that are, or were once, alive.
	cjones@isis.cs.du.edu (Charles J. Jones)


10) Holier than thou
Make no changes.  Let people limit themselves if they want limits.
	bis@chaos.cs.brandeis.edu (Bis)


11) Whoa!
Make certain items (i.e. wands of wonder), that would be unaffected
by polymorph, presumably due to their already being polymorphic.


12) Only the lonely
Allow only one wand of polymorph (generally, N wands) at a time in the game.
	marty@hpcuhb.cup.hp.com (Marty Freitas)


13) Round, round, git around
Make items have internal state such that they can only be polymorphed
once, or revert to their `original' form after the Nth polymorph.
	yucao@nntp-server.caltech.edu.UUCP (Yu Cao)


14) One-shot Wonder
Limit each polymorph wand to one (1) charge.
	norm@cfctech.cfc.com (Norman J. Meluch)


